        <div class="fade-in">
          <p class="about-tagline">Advanced surgical skill, a soldier&rsquo;s discipline, and a genuine belief in second chances.</p>

          <p>Dr. Matthew Phillips grew up in Mesa, Arizona, and never really left the Valley behind. <!-- CONFIRM: hometown (Livermore, CA / raised in Mesa, AZ) and high school. --> After earning his undergraduate degree at Arizona State University, he headed east to the New York University College of Dentistry, where he received his Doctorate of Dental Surgery in 2004. <!-- CONFIRM: ASU undergraduate degree and dates; NYU DDS, year 2004. --> More than two decades later, his experience runs the full length of the field &mdash; from everyday family checkups to some of the most complex full-arch implant reconstruction in modern dentistry.</p>

          <p>He founded 3rd Set Smiles in Tempe to practice the way he always believed dentistry should be done: unhurried, honest, and built entirely around the person in the chair. Cleanings, fillings, and crowns; simple or complex extractions, implants, and dentures &mdash; fixed and removable &mdash; comprehensive care under one roof, explained in plain language, with no pressure and no sales pitch.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>A Decade in the U.S. Army</h2>
          <p>Dr. Phillips served ten years as a dentist in the United States Army, caring for soldiers and their families through assignments in South Korea, Iraq, Hawaii, and Maryland. <!-- CONFIRM: total years of service and list of duty stations. --> Along the way he completed three years of advanced surgical training and developed a focus on implant dentistry and rebuilding smiles for patients with severe tooth loss &mdash; often far from the comfort of a private office. He separated from the Army as a Major with an honorable discharge, and was recognized with the Brigadier General Joseph L. Bernier Award for his contributions to the Army&rsquo;s trauma research. <!-- CONFIRM: length of surgical training program; final rank (Major) and discharge type; Bgen Joseph L. Bernier Award. --></p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in callout-box">
          <p>He didn&rsquo;t just learn full-arch implant surgery at the highest level &mdash; he went on to teach it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>Teaching the Next Generation of Implant Dentists</h2>
          <p>After his military career, Dr. Phillips refined his expertise in advanced implant techniques &mdash; including All-on-4&reg; and implant-retained dentures &mdash; and stepped into a role teaching others. As Surgical Training Advisor at Renew Anchored Dentures, founded by ClearChoice co-founder Dr. Don Miloni, he helped establish surgical protocols and trained practicing dentists in full-arch implant procedures. <!-- CONFIRM: exact title (Surgical Training Advisor / Director of Surgical Services) and tenure dates at Renew. --> The same hands that trained other clinicians in full-arch protocols now care for patients here in Tempe.</p>
        </div>

